+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage using native Web Components. No dependencies or build step are required. Load `components.js` as a module alongside `styles.css`.
+
+## Components
+
+- `<grind-navigation>` provides the responsive navigation disclosure with expanded state and Escape handling.
+- `<coffee-menu>` wraps any number of `<coffee-card>` elements. Its All / Hot / Iced buttons filter cards by their `category` attribute and announce the visible count.
+- `<coffee-card>` displays a coffee and opens a native modal dialog with keyboard dismissal, focus containment, and focus restoration. Attributes: `name`, `category` (`hot` or `iced`), `label`, `price`, `image`, `image-alt`, `description`, `notes`, and `details`. Attribute changes update the rendered card. Use descriptive image alternatives and ingredient/allergen information in `details`.
+- `<grind-rewards>` provides a native disclosure linking to the existing rewards route.
+
+All components own their markup, styles, and behavior in open Shadow DOM. Menu cards remain in the light DOM as slotted content. Components inherit the optional `--ink`, `--forest`, `--cream`, and `--serif` brand tokens; card content is escaped before rendering, and image URLs must use HTTP or HTTPS. Navigation and menu event listeners are removed when disconnected.
+
+The account, logout, ordering, locations, rewards, and footer URLs preserve the site's existing route conventions and require those pages to be supplied by the host application. This repository only contains the homepage.
+
+Syntax check: `node --check components.js`. There is no build script. Images are remotely hosted stock photos from Unsplash.
